======================================================================
  RANKING COMPRESSOR: Practical Pairwise Comparison Tool
======================================================================

  EXAMPLE 1: 6-team round-robin tournament
  Teams: A(0), B(1), C(2), D(3), E(4), F(5)
  Raw storage: 15 bits
  Compressed (tiling): 10 bits (1.50x)
  Score sequence: (0, 1, 3, 3, 3, 5)
  Regularity: 2.58 (0=regular, higher=more unequal)
  Three-cycles: 1 (0=transitive, higher=more cyclic)
  Base path valid: False
  Fingerprint: ((0, 1, 3, 3, 3, 5), 1, 1)

  SCALING TEST:
     N   Raw bits  Tiling bits   Ratio  Savings
     5         10            6   1.667        4
    10         45           36   1.250        9
    20        190          171   1.111       19
    50       1225         1176   1.042       49
   100       4950         4851   1.020       99

  DUPLICATE DETECTION:
  Tournament 1 fingerprint: ((2, 3, 3, 3, 4, 4, 4, 5), 7, 18)
  Tournament 2 fingerprint: ((2, 3, 3, 3, 4, 4, 4, 5), 8, 18)
  Same fingerprint (likely isomorphic): False

  APPLICATION DOMAINS:
  - Sports: Store 496 NFL matchup bits as 465 (save 31 bits)
  - Voting: 45 pairwise preferences -> 36 bits per ballot
  - ML: 4950 comparison matrix -> 4851 bits (99 fewer)
  - DB: Fingerprint-indexed tournament database for O(1) lookup

DONE.
